      "id": 1,
      "text": "Foster was first settled in 1717 before becoming an independent town in 1781 after separating from Scituate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://greenerpasture.com/Places/Details/1121"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Shortly before its incorporation, Foster’s first Calvinist Baptist church was founded, marking the town’s early religious roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foster%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Soon after, Six Principle Baptist and Free Will Baptist congregations were established, expanding the town’s diverse faith community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foster%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s name honors U.S. Senator Nelson Aldrich, who was born in Foster in 1841.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foster%2C_Rhode_Island"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Foster’s historic town hall, the Foster Town House, still serves as the center of local government.",
